  "description": "The SuperB titanium mountain bike was designed to be a hardtail bikepack race bike in the spirit of singletrack races. The design philosophy includes personal experience in the Arizona Trail Race and drawing from others’ experiences in long races. The multiple challenges of being in the saddle on a tough trail for 18 hours or more were taken into consideration.\n\nFor that reason, the SuperB demands as little as possible from the tired rider. It is responsive and agile on the trail, even while loaded. The SuperB has specific, but subtle, endurance features incorporated into it. For example, it has a longer front suspension and a taller stack. The rider has a more comfortable seated position and more front squish, as a result.\n\nIn addition, the SuperB has a lower top tube to ease throwing a leg over. Just think about all those hike-a-bike situations! The design is also mindful of bottom bracket height in chunky terrain. And, a heavy seatpost bag is no problem with the stouter seat stay/seat tube/top tube junction. Finally, the rider has a wide range of tire clearance options with the ability to run either 29″ up to 2.6 or 27.5″ up to 3.0.",
